One line in a lending fork's price oracle valued a stablecoin at a quintillionth of its price.

return 1;

The math this fork inherited expects every price as a mantissa: a number scaled by 1e18. One dollar is 1e18. A literal 1 is a quintillionth of a dollar.

The oracle had a special case for the protocol's own stablecoin market, and that branch returned 1.

Wrong: return 1;
Right: return 1e18;

Every collateral, borrow and liquidation calculation for that market multiplied by that price. The stablecoin counted for essentially nothing as collateral, so anyone posting it saw zero borrowing power.

It compiles. Static analyzers don't track units, so to them every uint256 is the same number.

